 notes='Atkin running page is read 9, with the older alternatives 8 and 6 retained as doubtful because of the intersecting head strokes; archive sheet 48. The page defines U_q on a Laurent/power series and applies its alpha-th iterate to j. It then takes q=19 and writes three congruences in a system labelled (4.1), with a double written plus at the line break of the third relation. The footnote says that the deeper modular theory also applies at q=13 but gives weaker results for the stated purpose. The closing paragraph says extra powers of 19 in the constants were established by actual computation and were necessary for the M- and R-results. It continues on scan50.\n\nS049-U-ITERATION: From the definition, the coefficient of x^n in U_q^alpha A is a(q^alpha n), by induction on alpha. Applied to the normalized j of scan43, for alpha≥1 the pole term x^-1 is killed because no integer n solves q^alpha n=-1; the zero constant term also remains zero. Hence the displayed sum beginning at n=1 is consistent in the positive-alpha range used here. No coefficient system g_n or modular-theoretic existence proof is supplied on this page, so those assertions are carried as background.\n\nThe typed slip a prioir is preserved with its exchange mark. The old j between R and results is cancelled and replaced by a hyphen, identified explicitly in the marginal (hyphen) note. The abbreviation R retains the meaning ramified established on scan47; the different expansion in C’s H63-06 auxiliary abbreviation list is not followed, and it is not counted as a transcription change.',
